```
I’m considering whether the abstract is absolutely necessary, so I might skip that.

Also, I need to clarify that my notation \(R\pi_*\) doesn’t conflict. I’ll define \(X\) and \(P\) clearly, and I realize I should mention that in additive notation, \(\mathbb{N}^2\) is written additively. 

There's a potential issue regarding referring to \(0 \cdot p(z) \le p(y)\) in the proof of Lemma 2.2 since using integer \(0\) is allowed in the definition of \(\prec\). I’ll be sure that it’s clear that integers \(m, n\) aren’t necessarily positive.

Lastly, I’ll confirm \(2p(z) - p(y) = 3(b - a) \in V\) holds if \(b \ge a\) and I’ll need to show \(p(z) \in V\) too, which I can do by similar reasoning. I think expressing monoids as semigroups additively keeps everything in order. All looks okay!
